      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    .article-pill-card {
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 1.25rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: space-between;
    }
    .article-pill-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
    }
    .article-pill-title {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #0a1128;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
    .article-pill-desc {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: #64748b;
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .article-pill-link {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--primary);
    }

    /* Footer */
    .pillar-footer {
      background: #ffffff;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      padding: 3rem 1.25rem;
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: 4rem;
    }
    .footer-social-bar {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.85rem;
      justify-content: center;
      margin: 1.25rem 0;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .social-btn {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 38px;
      height: 38px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Top Sticky Bar -->
  <header class="pillar-header">
    <div class="header-inner">
      <a href="/cng/" class="brand-link">
        <img src={brandLogo} alt={`${businessName} Logo`} style="width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 6px; object-fit: cover;" />
        <span>⚡ {businessName}</span>
      </a>
      <nav class="header-nav">
        <a href="#rules">Regulations</a>
        <a href="#procedure">Testing Procedure</a>
        <a href="#pump-refusal">Pump Rules</a>
        <a href="#faqs">FAQs</a>
        <a href="/cng/cylinder-test/" class="btn-header-cta">Book Testing Bay ({advanceFormatted} Advance) →</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="pillar-hero">
    <div class="hero-container">
      <span class="hero-badge">Statutory Educational Resource • Gas Cylinders Rules (2016)</span>
      
      <h1 class="hero-title">
        The Complete Guide to CNG Cylinder Hydro Testing in India
      </h1>

      <p class="hero-subtitle">
        Everything vehicle owners, fleet managers, and commercial operators must know about the mandatory 3-year hydrostatic stretch testing cycle, PESO Form C certification, and avoiding fuel station refusal.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-cta-group">
        <a href="/cng/cylinder-test/" class="btn-primary-cta">
          <span>⚡</span> Book Cylinder Test Bay ({advanceFormatted} Advance) →
        </a>
        <a href="/cng/cylinder-test/?action=check-due-date" class="btn-secondary-cta">
          <span>📅</span> Check Retest Due Date & Claim ₹200 Voucher
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Pillar Content -->
  <main class="pillar-layout">
    <article class="content-article">
      
      <div class="highlight-card">
        <strong>⚖️ Executive Regulatory Summary</strong>
        Under <strong>Rule 35 of the Gas Cylinders Rules (2016)</strong> and Indian Standard <strong>IS 8451</strong>, every CNG vehicle cylinder must undergo high-pressure water-jacket hydrostatic testing every <strong>3 years</strong>. Without an active compliance plate stamped by a PESO-certified testing facility, CNG pumps will reject refueling.
      </div>

      <h2 id="rules">1. Why CNG Cylinder Hydro Testing is Mandatory Every 3 Years</h2>
      <p>
        Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) is stored in automobile cylinders under extreme pressures between <strong>200 to 250 Bar (2,900 to 3,600 PSI)</strong>. Unlike liquid petroleum or diesel tanks which operate at atmospheric pressure, a CNG cylinder is a certified pressure vessel subjected to continuous stress cycles.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every time a vehicle refuels at a CNG station, the cylinder walls expand slightly under high pressure and contract as fuel is consumed during driving. Over 3 years of daily driving on Indian roads, road vibrations, thermal fluctuations, and pressure cycling can induce microscopic fatigue, valve seat degradation, or internal moisture-induced corrosion.
      </p>
      <p>
        The 3-year statutory retest is a life-safety mandate supervised by the <strong>Petroleum and Explosives Safety Organization (PESO)</strong>, Ministry of Commerce and Industry. Its purpose is to guarantee that the vessel has not exceeded its allowable elastic deformation and can safely withstand pressure spikes during fast-fill dispensing.
      </p>

      <h2 id="procedure">2. What Happens During the 300 Bar Water-Jacket Hydro Test</h2>
      <p>
        Hydrostatic stretch testing is performed using a high-precision calibrated water-jacket apparatus. The cylinder is submerged in water, sealed inside an armored jacket, and pressurized to <strong>300 Bar (1.5 times its working operating pressure)</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="procedure-step-grid">
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">1</span>
          <h4>Degassing & Depressurization</h4>
          <p>Residual natural gas is safely purged into a flare chimney or recovery system to ensure zero explosive vapor remains.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">2</span>
          <h4>Endoscopic Internal Inspection</h4>
          <p>An illuminated high-definition borescope is inserted into the cylinder neck to inspect the inner lining for pitting, rust, or oil contamination.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">3</span>
          <h4>300 Bar Water Jacket Test</h4>
          <p>The cylinder is filled with water, placed into the water jacket test rig, and pressurized to 300 Bar. Displaced jacket water is measured in a calibrated burette.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">4</span>
          <h4>Permanent Expansion Measurement</h4>
          <p>Upon pressure release, residual volumetric expansion is measured. By law, permanent expansion must not exceed 10% of total expansion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">5</span>
          <h4>Ultrasonic Wall Thickness Check</h4>
          <p>Multi-point ultrasonic thickness gauges measure cylinder wall thickness to ensure compliance with original manufacturer tolerances.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">6</span>
          <h4>Hot Air Drying & Valve Torquing</h4>
          <p>The interior is dried using heated dry air. The cylinder valve is overhauled, fitted with new O-rings, and torqued to specified foot-pounds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">7</span>
          <h4>Brass Compliance Plate Stamping</h4>
          <p>A tamper-evident compliance plate is engraved with testing plant identification, test pressure, retest date, and next expiry date.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">8</span>
          <h4>PESO Form C Certificate Generation</h4>
          <p>An official digital PESO Form C test certificate is generated and issued, linking the vehicle chassis number and cylinder serial number.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="pump-refusal">3. Why CNG Fuel Pumps Refuse Uncertified Vehicles</h2>
      <p>
        City Gas Distribution (CGD) companies such as Indraprastha Gas Limited (IGL), Haryana City Gas, Adani Total Gas, and Torrent Gas operate under strict safety guidelines. Pump attendants are legally mandated to inspect the brass compliance plate affixed near your vehicle's fueling inlet or under the bonnet before inserting the nozzle.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the compliance plate is missing, unreadable, or past its 3-year validity date:
      </p>
      <ul style="margin: 0 0 1.5rem 1.5rem; color: #475569; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <li><strong>Automated Refueling Shutoff:</strong> The station nozzle will not be connected.</li>
        <li><strong>No Counter Override:</strong> Attendants face criminal penalties and stations face license forfeiture if an uncertified vessel experiences rupture on pump premises.</li>
        <li><strong>Traffic Police Challans:</strong> Driving a CNG vehicle with an expired compliance plate violates the Motor Vehicles Act, carrying fines up to ₹10,000 and vehicle impoundment.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Transparent Pricing: Zero Retail Markups</h2>
      <p>
        Local roadside garages frequently act as middlemen, taking customer cars to distant testing facilities and adding substantial surcharges. Testing directly at an authorized Class-A PESO station guarantees transparent government-aligned pricing:
      </p>
      <ul style="margin: 0 0 1.5rem 1.5rem; color: #475569; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <li><strong>Single Cylinder (Private Car / Taxi):</strong> ₹2,500 base + 18% GST = ₹2,950 total.</li>
        <li><strong>Dual Cylinders (Commercial Vans / Tempo):</strong> ₹5,000 base + 18% GST = ₹5,900 total.</li>
        <li><strong>Four Cylinders (Heavy Commercial Trucks):</strong> ₹10,000 base + 18% GST = ₹11,800 total.</li>
        <li><strong>Online Advance:</strong> Flat {advanceFormatted} advance locks your designated bay, with remainder payable on delivery.</li>
      </ul>

      <div style="text-align: center; margin: 2.5rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: #f0f9ff; border: 1.5px solid #bae6fd; border-radius: 16px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #0369a1;">Need to Book Your 3-Year CNG Cylinder Hydro Test?</h3>
        <p style="color: #0c4a6e; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          Lock your preferred 20-minute arrival slot at our Rewari Class-A testing plant with express 2-hour turnaround.
        </p>
        <a href="/cng/cylinder-test/" class="btn-primary-cta" style="margin-right: 0.5rem;">
          Book Testing Bay ({advanceFormatted} Flat Advance) →
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="faqs">5. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item" open>
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>How often must a vehicle CNG cylinder be tested in India?</span>
            <span>▾</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-content">
            Under Rule 35 of the Gas Cylinders Rules (2016), on-board motor vehicle CNG cylinders must undergo hydrostatic stretch testing every 3 years from the date of initial manufacture or previous test.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>What happens if my cylinder fails the hydrostatic test?</span>
            <span>▾</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-content">
            If permanent volumetric expansion exceeds 10% or structural flaws are detected, the cylinder is condemned by the testing plant in accordance with PESO guidelines to ensure public safety. You will not be charged balance fees, and guidance on certified cylinder replacement is provided.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>What is the booking advance and cancellation policy?</span>
            <span>▾</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-content">
            Online reservations require a flat {advanceFormatted} advance to lock your designated express testing bay and technician allocation. Because the bay is held exclusively for your vehicle and unavailable to other motorists, the booking advance is strictly non-refundable upon slot confirmation. The remaining fee is settled upon test completion.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>What documents are required for testing?</span>
            <span>▾</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-content">
            Please bring a copy of your vehicle Registration Certificate (RC) and your previous hydro test certificate (if available). The chassis number and cylinder serial numbers are verified against your RC during check-in.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>Can I wait at the facility during testing?</span>
            <span>▾</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-content">
            Yes. Our facility features a clean, air-conditioned customer lounge with live telemetry displays showing your cylinder's 300-bar test readings in real time. Express turnaround is 90 to 120 minutes.
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

